+# G5 native FP16 efficient-attention admission
+
+Separate native FP16 policy/graph/weights/profile identities are required. Existing FP32 math/provider /1 digest bytes and behavior stay unchanged, including TF32off. No CPU profile becomes FP16, no W8-to-half artifact is accepted as original source proof, and no reference/resource/CAL verdict is retagged. The native metadata constructor emits unqualified data only, using actual source assets/current compiler and fresh unavailable CAL; actual EvaluationOwner/ServiceLease/device/context/charge/settlement remain required.
+
+The central Retrieval ORT initialization records inherited ORT_CUDA_GEMM_OPTIONS and ORT_ENABLE_ATTENTION_KERNEL_DEBUG_INFO before creating any OrtEnv (MiniLM can initialize first). It never writes environment variables. F16 requires snapshot and current values exactly2 and1, Unicode, and unchanged; a late setter cannot repair an earlier missing/conflicting snapshot. FP32 may run with the shared inherited settings without changing its /1 identity. F16 configures CUDA-only, error-on-failure, CPU fallback disabled, TF32off, CUDA graphoff, declared arena limit, and sdpa1 (Context Flash) or2 (Focus MEA). Requested options are not proof of actual backend.
+
+F16 external FLOAT16=10 values use existing locked half2.7.1 plus ort/half only under gpu-cuda. Values are loaded bit-for-bit from verified bytes, never re-rounded in native loader. Legacy external-data parser behavior remains; additive F16 audit validates all external shape/element/range lengths, disjoint ranges and at least one half initializer. CPU/default builds gain no half requirement. Scores/logits remain exactly F32 and original input ABI remains unchanged.
+
+Actual graph admission audits exact28 Focus/Compact or36 Large named efficient attention nodes, domain, operator, attributes, inputs/no cache/no bias/head128 scale, and native final SessionState placement must contain the complete same-node CUDA roster. Context masks are all-live sequential positions1..8192; Focus static512 accepts only nonempty live suffix with original0..511 positions. Every dispatch rechecks the original deadline, native input semantics and immutable math environment. Full learned weight conversion/protected FP32-island equivalence remains independent exporter/Torch/artifact qualification evidence; graph metadata alone is no such proof.
+
+Stock ORT debug output precedes kernel completion. Qualification must reconcile exact planned forward labels and complete node roster with actual fp16 FLASH_ATTENTION/Focus EFFICIENT_ATTENTION lines plus separately authenticated native return+GPU synchronization. Missing/MATH/foreign/duplicate/partial evidence refuses G5 qualification. Native input/output, all1..8192 structural compatibility, original FP32 and matching-half numeric bounds, genuine20 samples/allocator peaks/coexistence/cancel/OOM/task/CAL gates remain independent. No input budget, memory ceiling, tolerance, retry or clock is widened. No unqualified metadata grants public Auto/GPU admission.
+
+The data-only native constructor takes typed actual Core Assets, closed original graph lineage (Focus19b20/Compactc79/Largef8), actual source, native runtime manifest and declared phase plan. It authenticates current metadata/new graph+weights, creates new unavailable CAL, clears targets/qualification/downloads, retains current compiler/tokenizer/host tiers and emits distinct G5 manifest. It is not an execution capability. Its original source-lineage field and actual artifact bytes still require independent transformation and matching-half Torch proof; this constructor grants none.
+
+The artifact graph auditor additionally requires explicit Focus per-layer padded-query Where sanitization and live output32 edge, avoiding unwritten padded query outputs. Complete dtype/head/mask/full-model equivalence remains bound to the authenticated reviewed exporter and independent full initializer/cast-boundary proof. Actual stock backend logs and native returned+synchronized completion are mandatory independent evidence; no debug setting or attention plan means backend success.
+
+Ordinary product service launch still needs its owning safe child-spawn environment policy to inherit2/debug1 before ORT initialization. This Retrieval change never performs a late process environment setter. Missing/conflicting startup state refuses F16 and preserves existing qualified CPU/F32 fallback semantics. Public AutoF16 completion is not claimed by source review.
